# UI Charts and Visualisation Components

All custom chart components live in `apps/web/src/components/charts/`. All are client components.

## StatGauge
The most-reused component. Horizontal bar with green/amber/red zones and threshold tick marks.

```tsx
<StatGauge metric="wasserstein1" value={0.047} label="Wasserstein-1" />
```

- Reads `STAT_SCALES` from `lib/stats.ts` (generated from `_scales.py`). **Never hardcode thresholds inside the component.**
- Shows `pass`/`warn`/`fail` color based on verdict from the scale.
- Shows `plain_english_label` below the bar.
- Threshold tick positions are derived from `warn_threshold` and `fail_threshold`.
- `direction` ("lower_is_better" vs "higher_is_better") determines which end is red.

## StatChip
Inline compact gauge for table cells. Same scale logic as `StatGauge` but minimal — just a colored badge with the value.

```tsx
<StatChip metric="ks_2sample" value={0.12} />
```

## InfoTip
`(i)` icon + tooltip. Exposes the underlying stat method description from `STAT_SCALES.hint`.
```tsx
<InfoTip metric="wasserstein1" />
```

## Spark
Tiny inline SVG line chart (~60×20px) for sparklines in tables.
```tsx
<Spark data={scores} w={60} h={20} color="var(--accent)" />
```

## TimeSeries
Larger time series with confidence band, anomaly markers, changepoint verticals.
```tsx
<TimeSeries data={runs} band={ciData} anomalies={anomalyIndices} changepoints={cpDates} />
```

## HistDual
Overlapping histograms — current (orange/accent) over baseline (gray). Shows distribution shift visually.
```tsx
<HistDual a={currentBins} b={baselineBins} />
```

## CDFPair
Overlapping CDFs with KS supremum point marked. Used on the datasets detail screen alongside `HistDual`.
```tsx
<CDFPair a={currentCDF} b={baselineCDF} />
```

## KLMatrix
Symmetric heatmap of pairwise KL divergence across metrics. Diagonal masked.
```tsx
<KLMatrix metrics={metricNames} matrix={klValues} />
```

## CausalDAG
SVG DAG, bezier edges, weight + lag labels.
- Hover highlights upstream/downstream nodes.
- Click-to-select fires `onSelect(nodeId)`.
- Edge color encodes edge weight (green = strong, gray = weak).
- "Fragile" badge on edges with E-value < 1.5.

```tsx
<CausalDAG nodes={nodes} edges={edges} target="gmv_usd" onSelect={setSelected} />
```

## EngineGlyph
Per-engine SVG icon. One glyph per engine: Postgres, MySQL, BigQuery, ClickHouse, Snowflake, Redshift, Databricks, DuckDB, Trino.
```tsx
<EngineGlyph engine="postgres" size={24} />
```

## Chart principles
- All charts use SVG or canvas. No third-party chart library (recharts, etc.) — bespoke for the design system.
- Colors from CSS variables, not hardcoded hex.
- All charts are accessible: `aria-label` on the `<svg>`, a screen-reader-only `<caption>` with the key insight.
